  // ── P5c: exec playwright / playwright-test steps ─────────────────────
  //
  // INTENTIONALLY NOT GATED HERE (local-only / structural, like `run` and
  // `doctor`). The `playwright` and `playwright-test` step kinds drive a real
  // browser: they need Node + the `playwright` / `@playwright/test` npm
  // packages + a downloaded browser (~500MB). That tool surface is NOT present
  // hermetically on the conformance runners, so a browser-dependent scenario
  // cannot be byte-gated in CI without making the gate flaky / non-hermetic —
  // the same reason `doctor` (PATH-dependent) and `run` (live test runners) are
  // excluded above.
  //
  // What IS verified, and where:
  //   - The GRACEFUL-TOOL-ABSENT path (the only hermetic part) — when
  //     `@playwright/test` is missing, `npx playwright test` exits non-zero
  //     without writing the JUnit XML, so the step errors with Go's exact
  //     "playwright-test failed to produce JUnit XML: read junit xml <tmp>:
  //     open <tmp>: no such file or directory; cmd exit: exit status 1" wording
  //     (volatile tmp path + stderr aside). Confirmed byte-identical to the Go
  //     oracle during the P5c parity diff.
  //   - The hermetic sub-paths are gated by `moon test` (executor wbtests):
  //     the embedded harness is byte-identical to harness/playwright.mjs (diff
  //     test), base64 matches Go base64.StdEncoding (RFC vectors), the JUnit XML
  //     parse + outcome aggregation (pass/fail/skip/error buckets), the console
  //     substring assertions, the screenshot %.2f diff formatting, and the
  //     no-spec / script-not-found graceful errors.
  //   - The LIVE browser path was smoke-tested LOCALLY against examples/
  //     playwright-{page,console,screenshot,test-suite} with a real chromium +
  //     `@playwright/test`: byte-identical outcomes + reasons to the Go oracle,
  //     and the written screenshot PNG was byte-identical (same MD5). This
  //     local smoke is NOT part of the CI net (no browser on the runners).
  //
  // P4c exec-shard-balanced: `exec --shard 1/4` over the 10-test shard-balanced
  // example, with a COMMITTED .pkspec/timings.jsonl (fixed per-test durations:
  // fast=50ms, mid=150ms, slow=400ms). LPT bin-packing of those durations is
  // deterministic, so shard 1/4 always selects EXACTLY {fast_a, fast_d, slow_a}
  // and only those three run. Gates the LPT selection + the shard banner +
  // per-test progress + summary (exactStderr + normalizeDurations). Both
  // binaries pick the identical subset (LPT parity). PASSES, exit 0.
  new {
    id = "exec-shard-balanced"
    fixture = "conformance/fixtures/exec-shard-balanced"
    env { ["PKF_CONFORMANCE_SUBDIR"] = "examples/shard-balanced" }
    argv { "exec"; "-f"; "Test.pkl"; "--shard"; "1/4"; "--no-record-timings" }
    contract = new {
      exit = true
      stdoutEmpty = true
      exactStderr = true
      normalizeDurations = true
    }
  }
  // P4c exec-rerun-failed: `exec --rerun-failed` over shard-balanced with a
  // COMMITTED timings.jsonl whose MOST-RECENT (ts-desc) local records are:
  // fast_a=fail, mid_c=skip, slow_b=error (selected); fast_b=pass (excluded);
  // slow_c=pass but env=ci (excluded by env filter); all other tests have no
  // history (excluded). So exactly {fast_a, mid_c, slow_b} re-run — a stable
  // set proving the most-recent + env-filter + isFailedOutcome (fail/error/skip)
  // logic. Gates the rerun banner + selection + summary (exactStderr +
  // normalizeDurations). PASSES (the bodies are sleeps), exit 0.
  new {
    id = "exec-rerun-failed"
    fixture = "conformance/fixtures/exec-rerun-failed"
    env { ["PKF_CONFORMANCE_SUBDIR"] = "examples/shard-balanced" }
    argv { "exec"; "-f"; "Test.pkl"; "--rerun-failed"; "--no-record-timings" }
    contract = new {
      exit = true
      stdoutEmpty = true
      exactStderr = true
      normalizeDurations = true
    }
  }
  // P4c exec-total-timeout: `exec --total-timeout 1ms` over shard-balanced.
  // The first test (fast_a, `sleep 0.05` = 50ms) cannot finish inside a 1ms
  // wall-clock cap, so the shared deadline aborts it mid-body — Go's ctx kills
  // the subprocess and cmdExec overrides the reason to "aborted by
  // total-timeout" (Errored); every subsequent test is marked Skipped with
  // "not executed: context deadline exceeded". Deterministic because 50ms >> 1ms
  // always. Gates the per-test errored/skipped lines + the [timeout] line +
  // summary (exactStderr + normalizeDurations) + exit 1 (skipped → red).
  new {
    id = "exec-total-timeout"
    fixture = "conformance/fixtures/exec-total-timeout"
    env { ["PKF_CONFORMANCE_SUBDIR"] = "examples/shard-balanced" }
    argv {
      "exec"
      "-f"
      "Test.pkl"
      "--total-timeout"
      "1ms"
      "--no-record-timings"
    }
    contract = new {
      exit = true
      stdoutEmpty = true
      exactStderr = true
      normalizeDurations = true
    }
